SUBJ/TROPICAL CYCLONE FORMATION ALERT REISSUED //
WTPN21 PHNC 130630
REF/A/JOINT TYPHOON WRNCEN PEARL HARBOR HI/120621Z OCT 26//
AMPN/REF IS TROPICAL CYCLONE FORMATION ALERT (WTPN21 PHNC 120630)//
RMKS/
1. FORMATION OF A SIGNIFICANT TROPICAL CYCLONE IS POSSIBLE WITHIN
120 NM EITHER SIDE OF A LINE FROM 8.3N 95.1W TO 10.6N 99.8W
WITHIN THE NEXT 12 TO 24 HOURS. AVAILABLE DATA DOES NOT JUSTIFY
ISSUANCE OF NUMBERED TROPICAL CYCLONE WARNINGS AT THIS TIME.
WINDS IN THE AREA ARE ESTIMATED TO BE 23 TO 27 KNOTS. METSAT
IMAGERY AT 130600Z INDICATES THAT A CIRCULATION CENTER IS LOCATED
NEAR 8.3N 95.3W. THE SYSTEM IS MOVING WESTWARD AT 14 KNOTS.
2. REMARKS:
MAXIMUM SUSTAINED SURFACE WINDS ARE ESTIMATED AT 23 TO 27 KNOTS.
MINIMUM SEA LEVEL PRESSURE IS ESTIMATED TO BE NEAR 1002 MB. THE
POTENTIAL FOR THE DEVELOPMENT OF A SIGNIFICANT TROPICAL CYCLONE
WITHIN THE NEXT 24 HOURS IS HIGH. THIS SUPERSEDES REF A.
3. THIS ALERT WILL BE REISSUED, UPGRADED TO WARNING OR CANCELLED BY 140630Z.
